From: Zylos <audit>
Subject: [PATCH] emblem-fury: stop the stale mobile-detect line from killing the page on phones

Round 10, domrun.mjs. On any mobile user agent the top-level detect block threw
TypeError on a null #mobile-overlay -- an id this page no longer defines -- before
the bootstrap 'load' listener at the bottom of the file was ever registered. So
showCharacterSelect() and requestAnimationFrame(gameLoop) never ran: the game was
dead on every phone, not merely missing its touch controls.

Nothing of value is removed. Visibility is CSS (@media max-width:800px,
(pointer:coarse) on .mobile-controls-container), and the load handler already
calls setupMobileControls() with a broader condition ('ontouchstart' in window).
The block was a leftover from before the mobile layer was rewritten -- the
surviving setupMobileControls() at line 2798 already uses the correct ids and
guards them.

Verified: mobile 'load' listener count 0 -> 1; click/keydown wiring now matches
desktop exactly (2/4 on both). No desktop change.

--- a/emblem-fury.html
+++ b/emblem-fury.html
@@ -2743,11 +2743,9 @@
   document.getElementById('btn-pause')?.addEventListener('click',togglePause);
 }
 
-// Detect mobile
-if(/Mobi|Android|iPhone|iPad/i.test(navigator.userAgent)){
-  document.getElementById('mobile-overlay').style.display='block';
-  setupMobileControls();
-}
+// Mobile detection intentionally lives in the load handler at the bottom of this
+// file. The container is revealed by CSS (@media max-width:800px,(pointer:coarse)),
+// so there is nothing for JS to show here.
 
 // ── INIT + START GAME ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 function initGame(){
